# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Niccolò Di Eugenio et al. (2025). Machine-Learned Interatomic Potentials for Structural and Defect Properties of YBa$_2$Cu$_3$O$_{7-δ}$.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2511.22592  arXiv:2511.22592v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2511.22592v2 (sha256 0cd4f81c7728607d...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 289 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/eugenio2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the YBCO DFT database built here (2,712 structures of
# YBCO7, YBCO6, Y, Ba, Cu, O and binary oxides with volume, strain, thermal,
# defect and amorphous perturbations plus active learning), the YBCO ACE,
# MACE, GAP and tabGAP potentials trained on it, their validation RMSEs
# printed in Fig. 3 and the MD speeds of Table I. Lattice parameters,
# elastic, thermal-expansion, defect and NEB results are properties, not
# error metrics.

